<onlyinclude>A '''cyborg''' (cybernetic organism) is an organism integrated with technological components that support or modify its functions. The term was introduced by Manfred Clynes and Nathan Kline in 1960 in the context of space travel.

== Explanation ==
Examples of biological–technological integration include implanted devices that support heart function or provide sensory input. Different uses of the term vary in how closely the technology must interact with the body. Cultural theorists also use cyborg as a metaphor for hybrid identities; that is distinct from an engineering definition.

